>> title: Italian Sausage Lentil Soup
>> servings: 8
>> source: Sara

Cook @sweet italian sausage{1%lb}(casings removed) in #soup pot{} over medium-high heat, stirring often, until the meat crumbles and begins to brown, about ~{4%minutes}.

Add @onion{1%cup}(chopped) and @garlic{2%cloves}(minced) and cook until onion softens and sausage is browned all over, about ~{4%minutes} more.

Add @chicken stock{4%cups}, stirring and scraping to loosen the fond from the bottom of the pot.

Add @dried red lentils{2%cups}(rinsed), @whole peeled tomatoes{1%28oz can}, @salt{1%teaspoon}, @pepper{0.5%teaspon} and bring to a boil.

Reduce heat to medium-low and simmer until the lentils have softened, ~{20-25%minutes}.

Stir in @kale{5%cups}(roughly chopped) and cook, stirring constantly, until softened, about ~{1%minute}.